{"session_id":"svc-1778571630378942592","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-12T07:40:40.493950902Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"gpt-5.5","sticky":{"key_present":true,"bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"requested_harness":"codex","resolved_harness":"codex","harness_source":"request_harness","requested_model":"gpt-5.5","resolved_model":"gpt-5.5","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-72d18004-20260512T074027-ed0936a6","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead inside an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the completion contract — every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file you can point to after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs as separate deliverables.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized sub-pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, treat Step 0 as a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, decomposed children once more; third-level splits must be rejected with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose — do not attempt the work:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child slice (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `.ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6/no_changes_rationale.txt` listing child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A clean decomposition is a success. Do not mix implementation with decomposition.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC against concrete evidence (test name, file path, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `.ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6/no_changes_rationale.txt` (what is done, what blocks, what a follow-up needs) before exiting. No commit and no rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`. A well-justified no_changes beats a bad commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;`.ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6/no_changes_rationale.txt` must contain one:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` reject.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;To request orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Freestanding artifacts (investigation reports, findings docs) go under `.ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and project defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-72d18004\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003ebench: matrix runner halts lane after 5 consecutive identical failures\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nAdd a consecutive-failure halt to the matrix runner (cmd/bench/matrix.go) that aborts the entire lane after N=5 cells fail with byte-identical error fingerprints in a row. Writes a single `lane_aborted` summary cell explaining why; subsequent cells in the lane are skipped (not run, not written).\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Why this matters: see parent epic. The preflight smoke test (sibling bead fizeau-586e476a) catches misconfigured lanes at sweep startup. This bead is the defense-in-depth piece for cases where preflight passed but the endpoint dies mid-sweep — e.g. vLLM model engine enters a degraded state after running fine for a while, or a model server gets OOM-killed and the wrapper restarts it broken. Today such regressions cause every remaining cell in the lane to fail identically until human intervention.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Behavior:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- After each cell in a lane completes, compute a fingerprint = SHA256 of the report\u0026#39;s `error` field (truncated to first 256 bytes) + `final_status`. Store the last N=5 fingerprints in lane-scoped state inside the existing per-lane matrix runner process (no on-disk state).\u0026#xA;- When 5 consecutive cells share the same fingerprint AND are all `graded_fail` or `harness_crash` (not `graded_pass`), halt the lane:\u0026#xA;  * Write one synthetic `report.json` to a path like `\u0026lt;cells_root\u0026gt;/.lane_aborted/\u0026lt;lane_id\u0026gt;/aborted.json` with `final_status: \u0026#34;lane_aborted\u0026#34;`, `error: \u0026#34;halted after 5 consecutive identical failures: \u0026lt;fingerprint preview\u0026gt;\u0026#34;`, plus the fingerprint and the list of the 5 task ids that triggered.\u0026#xA;  * Print `[matrix] lane=\u0026lt;lane_id\u0026gt; ABORTED after 5 consecutive identical failures (last task: \u0026lt;task\u0026gt;): \u0026lt;error preview\u0026gt;` to stderr.\u0026#xA;  * Exit the matrix runner with a distinct exit code (e.g. 75 / EX_TEMPFAIL) so the sweep script can attribute the abort to this cause vs a normal lane completion.\u0026#xA;- Add `final_status: \u0026#34;lane_aborted\u0026#34;` to the matrix invalid-class machinery so the website / aggregates display these explicitly (not as silent missing cells).\u0026#xA;- Add a `--no-consecutive-failure-halt` flag to disable the safety net for operators debugging a known-broken lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Failure-mode test cases (must all be covered):\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- 5 cells with identical `agent: provider error: ...` errors → halt fires.\u0026#xA;- 5 cells with identical `harness_crash: context canceled` (the docker subnet exhaustion pattern from earlier in this codebase) → halt fires.\u0026#xA;- 4 identical errors then 1 graded_pass → halt does NOT fire; counter resets.\u0026#xA;- 4 identical errors then a 5th error with even one byte different → halt does NOT fire.\u0026#xA;- `--no-consecutive-failure-halt` flag → halt never fires regardless.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;In-scope files:\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/matrix.go — add ConsecutiveFailureTracker (or inline state) inside the matrix-runner main loop; integrate into the per-cell write path; add the flag.\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/matrix_invalid.go — register `lane_aborted` as a known invalid class (so summarizeMatrixCells counts it correctly, and the regen pipeline treats it as systemic, not model failure).\u0026#xA;- cmd/bench/matrix_test.go — add the four behavior tests above using the existing test fixture pattern.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Out-of-scope (file separate beads):\u0026#xA;- Auto-restart of the lane after the user fixes the issue. (For now, operator manually re-runs.)\u0026#xA;- Cross-lane abort cascade (one lane\u0026#39;s repeated failures shouldn\u0026#39;t halt other lanes).\u0026#xA;- Surfacing the halt count in the website data — that\u0026#39;s a follow-up once we see how often this fires in practice.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Acceptance is a command:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `go test ./cmd/bench/... -run TestConsecutiveFailureHalt` passes (covers the four behaviors above).\u0026#xA;2. With a deliberately-misconfigured fixture profile that produces identical errors, `fiz-bench matrix --profiles broken-fixture --reps 10 --out /tmp/abort-test` exits with code 75 after exactly 5 cells, writes `aborted.json` under `\u0026lt;out\u0026gt;/.lane_aborted/`, and the remaining 5 cells are not present in the output dir.\u0026#xA;3. The same fixture with `--no-consecutive-failure-halt` runs all 10 cells to completion (each failing) without aborting.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. go test ./cmd/bench/... -run TestConsecutiveFailureHalt covers the four behaviors above and passes. 2. Misconfigured fixture sweep exits code 75 after exactly 5 cells with aborted.json written. 3. --no-consecutive-failure-halt runs all cells without aborting. 4. lane_aborted appears as a known invalid class in matrix.json\u0026#39;s invalid_by_class breakdown.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:benchmark, kind:reliability, kind:hardening\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-1a5353cd\" base-rev=\"6fc99c64f379fcae9a9c41be21b23c569e1ca1cd\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read those before editing. Ground decisions in what is already in the repository; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","attempt_id":"20260512T074027-ed0936a6","base_rev":"6fc99c64f379fcae9a9c41be21b23c569e1ca1cd","bead_id":"fizeau-72d18004","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6","correlation_id":"fizeau-72d18004:20260512T074027-ed0936a6","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260512T074027-ed0936a6/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"1e9f097670d68700dd45f0e21d3c27e0d33fc486d75197a9944ec376ca10b47f","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-2a18ac4f","worker_id":""}}}
